<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>CT-1 Template</title>
    <style>
        @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
        .page {
            width: 794px; height: 1123px;
            padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
            overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
            position: relative;
            font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
        }
        .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
        table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 15px; }
        td { padding: 5px 0; }
        .header-title { font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px; }
        .section-heading { font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
        .form-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 10px; }
        .form-label { width: 30%; }
        .form-input { width: 65%; border-bottom: 1px solid #000; }
        .two-column-section { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 20px; }
        .two-column-section > div { width: 48%; }
        .signature-block { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 50px; }
        .signature-box { width: 45%; border-top: 1px solid #000; padding-top: 5px; }
        .instruction-box { font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4; margin-top: 20px; }
        .bold { font-weight: bold; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div>
            <div class="header-title">CT-1</div>
            <div style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10px;">Department of the Treasury</div>
            <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Internal Revenue Service</div>
        </div>
        <div style="text-align: right;">
            <div style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">OMB No. 1545-0001</div>
            <div style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">{{ current_year }}</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div class="form-row">
            <div class="form-label">Name</div>
            <div class="form-input"><span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="form-row">
            <div class="form-label">Employer identification number (EIN)</div>
            <div class="form-input"><span data-field="employer.ein">{{ employer.ein }}</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div class="form-row">
            <div class="form-label">Please type or print.</div>
            <div class="form-input"><span data-field="address_name">{{ address_name }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="form-row">
            <div class="form-label">Address (number and street)</div>
            <div class="form-input"><span data-field="address_street">{{ address_street }}</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div class="form-row">
            <div class="form-label">City, state, and ZIP code</div>
            <div class="form-input"><span data-field="address_city_state_zip">{{ address_city_state_zip }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="form-row">
            <div class="form-label">RRB number</div>
            <div class="form-input"><span data-field="rrb_number">{{ rrb_number }}</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div class="form-row">
            <div class="form-label">Calendar year</div>
            <div class="form-input"><span data-field="calendar_year">{{ calendar_year }}</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="form-row" style="justify-content: flex-end;">
            <div style="width: 30%;"></div>
            <div style="width: 30%;"></div>
            <div style="width: 30%; text-align: right;">
                If final return, check here. <input type="checkbox">
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-heading">Part I Railroad Retirement Taxes. On lines 1 through 10 below, enter the amount of compensation for each tax. Then, multiply it by the rate shown and enter the tax.</div>

    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <td style="width: 5%;"></td>
                <td style="width: 50%;">Compensation</td>
                <td style="width: 20%;">Rate</td>
                <td style="width: 25%;">Tax</td>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for i in range(1, 11) %}
            <tr>
                <td>{{ i }}</td>
                <td>
                    <span data-field="compensation_amount_{{ i }}">{{ compensation_amount_i }}</span>
                </td>
                <td>
                    <span data-field="rate_{{ i }}">{{ rate_value_{{ i }} }}%</span>
                </td>
                <td>
                    <span data-field="tax_amount_{{ i }}">{{ tax_value_{{ i }} }}</span>
                </td>
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="form-row" style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <div class="form-label">Total tax based on compensation (add lines 1 through 10).</div>
        <div class="form-input"><span data-field="total_tax_compensation">{{ total_tax_compensation }}</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="form-row" style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <div class="form-label">Adjustments to employer and employee railroad retirement taxes based on compensation. See the instructions for lines 12 and 13 and attached required statements.</div>
        <div class="form-input"><span data-field="adjustment_amount">{{ adjustment_amount }}</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="form-row" style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <div class="form-label">Fractions of cents $</div>
        <div class="form-input"><span data-field="fraction_of_cents">{{ fraction_of_cents }}</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Other $</div>
        <div class="form-input" style="width: 15%;"><span data-field="other_amount">{{ other_amount }}</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="form-row" style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <div class="form-label">Total railroad retirement taxes based on compensation (line 11 adjusted by line 12).</div>
        <div class="form-input"><span data-field="total_tax_adjusted_compensation">{{ total_tax_adjusted_compensation }}</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="form-row" style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <div class="form-label">Total railroad retirement taxes deposited for the year, including overpayment applied from a prior year and overpayment applied from Form CT-1 X.</div>
        <div class="form-input"><span data-field="total_tax_deposited">{{ total_tax_deposited }}</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="form-row" style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <div class="form-label">Balance due (subtract line 14 from line 13). Pay to the "United States Treasury" (see instructions).</div>
        <div class="form-input"><span data-field="balance_due">{{ balance_due }}</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="instruction-box">
        Pay using EFTPS or complete Form CT-1(V), Payment Voucher, and enclose with return and payment.
        <br>
        Overpayment. If line 14 is more than line 13, enter overpayment here <span data-field="overpayment_amount">{{ overpayment_amount }}</span> and check if you want it: <input type="checkbox"> Applied to next return or <input type="checkbox"> Refunded.
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div>
            <div class="section-heading">Part II Record of Railroad Retirement Tax Liability</div>
        </div>
        <div style="text-align: right;">
            <div style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">Page 2</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="instruction-box">
        Complete the Monthly Summary of Railroad Retirement Tax Liability below only if you were a <span data-field="monthly_schedule_depositor">{{ monthly_schedule_depositor }}</span> for the entire year. Enter your Tier I and Tier II tax liability on the lines provided for each month.
    </div>

    <div class="instruction-box">
        On Form 945-A for each payday, enter the sum of your employee and employer Tier I and Tier II taxes on the appropriate line.
        <br>
        Your total tax liability for the year (line V below or line M on Form 945-A) should equal your total taxes for the year (line 13, Form CT-1). Otherwise, you may be charged a failure-to-deposit penalty.
        <br>
        Note: See the instructions for the deposit rules for railroad retirement taxes.
    </div>

    <div class="section-heading">Monthly Summary of Railroad Retirement Tax Liability</div>

    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <td style="width: 20%;"></td>
                <td style="width: 10%;">First Quarter</td>
                <td style="width: 10%;">Second Quarter</td>
                <td style="width: 10%;">Third Quarter</td>
                <td style="width: 10%;">Fourth Quarter</td>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>Tier I and Tier II taxes <br> First month liability</td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q1_m1">{{ tier_i_ii_q1_m1 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q2_m1">{{ tier_i_ii_q2_m1 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q3_m1">{{ tier_i_ii_q3_m1 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q4_m1">{{ tier_i_ii_q4_m1 }}</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Second month of quarter:</td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q1_m2">{{ tier_i_ii_q1_m2 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q2_m2">{{ tier_i_ii_q2_m2 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q3_m2">{{ tier_i_ii_q3_m2 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q4_m2">{{ tier_i_ii_q4_m2 }}</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Tier I and Tier II taxes <br> Second month liability</td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q1_m2_label">{{ tier_i_ii_q1_m2_label }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q2_m2_label">{{ tier_i_ii_q2_m2_label }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q3_m2_label">{{ tier_i_ii_q3_m2_label }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q4_m2_label">{{ tier_i_ii_q4_m2_label }}</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Third month of quarter:</td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q1_m3">{{ tier_i_ii_q1_m3 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q2_m3">{{ tier_i_ii_q2_m3 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q3_m3">{{ tier_i_ii_q3_m3 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q4_m3">{{ tier_i_ii_q4_m3 }}</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Tier I and Tier II taxes <br> Third month liability</td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q1_m3_label">{{ tier_i_ii_q1_m3_label }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q2_m3_label">{{ tier_i_ii_q2_m3_label }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q3_m3_label">{{ tier_i_ii_q3_m3_label }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="tier_i_ii_q4_m3_label">{{ tier_i_ii_q4_m3_label }}</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>IV Total for quarter, add lines I, II, and III.</td>
                <td><span data-field="quarter_total_q1">{{ quarter_total_q1 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="quarter_total_q2">{{ quarter_total_q2 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="quarter_total_q3">{{ quarter_total_q3 }}</span></td>
                <td><span data-field="quarter_total_q4">{{ quarter_total_q4 }}</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>V Total railroad retirement tax liability for the year. This should equal Part I, line 13.</td>
                <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="annual_total_q1">{{ annual_total_q1 }}</span></td>
                <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="annual_total_q2">{{ annual_total_q2 }}</span></td>
                <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="annual_total_q3">{{ annual_total_q3 }}</span></td>
                <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="annual_total_q4">{{ annual_total_q4 }}</span></td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div>
            <div class="section-heading">Form CT-1(V), Payment Voucher</div>
        </div>
        <div style="text-align: right;">
            <div style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">Page 3</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="instruction-box">
        <p><strong>Purpose of Form</strong></p>
        <p>Complete Form CT-1(V), Payment Voucher, if you are making a payment with Form CT-1, Employer's Annual Railroad Retirement Tax Return. We will use the completed Form CT-1(V) to credit your payment more promptly and accurately, and to improve our service to you.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="instruction-box">
        <p><strong>Specific Instructions</strong></p>
        <p><strong>Box 1 - Employer identification number (EIN).</strong> Use the EIN from Form CT-1. If you do not have an EIN, you may apply for one online. Go to the IRS website at www.irs.gov/businesses/small-biz/apply-for-ein. You may also apply for an EIN by calling 1-800-829-4933, or you can fax or mail Form SS-4, Application for Employer Identification Number, to the IRS.</p>
        <p><strong>Box 2 - Amount paid.</strong> Enter the amount paid with Form CT-1.</p>
        <p><strong>Box 3 - Name and address.</strong> Enter your business name and address as shown on Form CT-1.</p>
        <p>• Enclose your check or money order made payable to the "United States Treasury." Be sure to enter your EIN, "Form CT-1," and the tax period on your check or money order. <span data-field="payment_instructions_note">{{ payment_instructions_note }}</span></p>
        <p>• Detach Form CT-1(V) and send it with your payment and Form CT-1 to the address in the Instructions for Form CT-1.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
            <div style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">&darr; Detach Here and Mail With Your Payment and Form CT-1 &darr;</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="border: 2px solid #000; padding: 20px; margin-top: 20px;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
            <div>
                <div style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Form CT-1(V)</div>
                <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Department of the Treasury</div>
                <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Internal Revenue Service</div>
            </div>
            <div style="text-align: right;">
                <div style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">OMB No. 1545-0001</div>
                <div style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">{{ current_year }}</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <div class="form-row">
                <div class="form-label">1 Enter your employer identification number (EIN)</div>
                <div class="form-input"><span data-field="payment_ein">{{ payment_ein }}</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="form-row">
                <div class="form-label">2 Enter the amount of your payment.</div>
                <div class="form-input" style="width: 30%;"><span data-field="payment_dollars">{{ payment_dollars }}</span></div>
                <div class="form-input" style="width: 10%;"><span data-field="payment_cents">{{ payment_cents }}</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="form-row">
                <div class="form-label">3 Enter your business name.</div>
                <div class="form-input"><span data-field="payment_business_name">{{ payment_business_name }}</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="form-row">
                <div class="form-label">Enter your address.</div>
                <div class="form-input"><span data-field="payment_address_street">{{ payment_address_street }}</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="form-row">
                <div class="form-label">Enter your city, state, and ZIP code.</div>
                <div class="form-input"><span data-field="payment_address_city_state_zip">{{ payment_address_city_state_zip }}</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div>
            <div class="section-heading">Form CT-1(V), Payment Voucher</div>
        </div>
        <div style="text-align: right;">
            <div style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">Page 4</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="instruction-box">
        <p><strong>Privacy Act and Paperwork Reduction Act Notice.</strong></p>
        <p>For action on this form to carry out the Internal Revenue Laws of the United States. You are required to give us this information. We need it to ensure that you are complying with these laws and to allow us to figure and collect the right amount of tax. Our authority to collect this information is found in the Internal Revenue Code, Section 6102(a) and their regulations. Section 6109 requires you to provide your identifying number on the return. If you do not provide the information we ask for, or provide false or misleading information, you may be subject to penalties.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="instruction-box">
        <p>Its instructions must be retained as long as their contents may become material in the administration of any Internal Revenue law. Generally, tax returns and return information are confidential, as required by section 6103.</p>
        <p>The time needed to complete and file Form CT-1 will vary depending on individual circumstances. The estimated average time is: <span data-field="estimated_time">{{ estimated_time }}</span>.</p>
        <p>Recordkeeping: 8 hr., 36 min.; Learning about the law or the form: 7 hr., 7 min.; Preparing, copying, assembling, and sending the form to the IRS: 4 hr., 4 min.</p>
        <p>If you have comments concerning the accuracy of these time estimates or suggestions for making Form CT-1 simpler, we would be happy to hear from you. You can write to the Internal Revenue Service, Tax Products Coordinating Committee, SEW/CARP: T.M.S. 1111, Washington, DC 20530. Please do not send Form CT-1 to this address. Instead, see Where To File in the Instructions for Form CT-1.</p>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>